<title>USA: Banyan shares cease trading on NYSE.</title>
<headline>Banyan shares cease trading on NYSE.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banyan Mortgage Investment Fund said its stock ceased trading on the New York Stock Exchange with the close of Tuesday's session.</p>
<p>Earlier, the company's shareholders approved a merger with RGI U.S. Holdings and a 25-for-one reverse stock split.</p>
<p>The merged company will operate under the name Legend Properties Inc and open for trading on the Nasdaq on January 2 under the symbol &quot;LPRO.&quot;</p>
<p>Legend, which plans to develop residential and commercial properties, will be located in Seattle.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
